WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.810
Like a silver shooting star,

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.610
Jenny Dolittle suddenly arrives at the Bentenmaru.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:10.370
Swept up in a struggle with her uncle
for the fate of her family's company,

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.650
Hugh and Dolittle, and forced into an unwanted marriage,

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.740
she seeks refuge on the Bentenmaru.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.080
With Jenny and Lynn's fate,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.040
and her own luck and future
as a pirate captain hanging in the balance,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.000
Marika decided to help Jenny.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.000
Then let's take them out.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:32.010
What is the captain of the Bentenmaru,
Kato Marika, asking them to do?

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.610
Omni-directional scan complete.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.820
I'm already seeing two to three pre-drives.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:16.780
Roger.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.110
Everyone seems really used to this.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.490
They're like real pirates.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.830
Well, we've been through a lot.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.160
Crew aside, this is a real pirate ship.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.420
How are you enjoying the ship you hired?

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.300
It's great!

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.720
Once I graduate, maybe I'll go into piracy.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.890
You can't get a pirate license anymore.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.220
They don't issue new ones.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.680
I've heard there are ways around that.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.520
Well, you can decide your post-graduation life later.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.810
For now, let's focus on what we're doing—

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.110
What's going on?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.070
The enemy's caught us!

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.900
Hugh and Dolittle's escort fleet...

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.280
Two Talbot-class and five Corback-class escorts.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.660
I thought we'd ditched them,
but they've already surrounded us.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.960
One more.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.790
The battleship Jabberwocky.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.340
I figured he'd show.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.800
So that's their big one.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:28.810
What happened?

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.640
Bombardment from five o'clock!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.730
Bombardment?

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.350
What will happen to us?

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.810
If it doesn't hit us, it can't hurt us.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.400
Energy readings?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.320
Eight.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.240
Calculating attack patterns.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.900
President, what about our electronic warfare?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.940
On it.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.490
Ai,

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.490
can you keep dodging a while longer?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.490
I'll try.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:47.910
Are you returning fire?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.000
No...

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.710
If we attack and hurt them,

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.540
we'll give them a leg up.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.340
That will disadvantage us in negotiations.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.750
All right.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.840
I'll back your decision.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.760
My uncle will wait for a bit to see what we do.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.390
So let's think of a plan.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.100
Robert Dolittle.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:16.980
Board member, Hugh and Dolittle
Interstellar Transportation Company.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.690
Also, my uncle.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.450
For years, he's been fighting my father, his younger brother,

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.200
for company control.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.450
Ever since I started the Fairy Jane travel company,

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.540
it's gotten worse.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.420
Ready to commence attack.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.080
Fire.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.590
Mr. Robert, we've already fired enough warning shots!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:42.090
If anything happens to her, the rest of the family...

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.510
Did you not hear me?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.720
I said fire.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:48.350
Yes, sir.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.890
Prepare to fire!

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:08.830
We have to hurry.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.780
Um,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.040
Jenny.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.080
What is it?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:16.670
Can you think of any weaknesses your uncle might have?

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.960
Let me see...

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.550
Weaknesses...

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:25.760
If there were something that only you, his niece, might know...

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.470
Nope.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.680
Attacking head-on is out of the question.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.850
It would be great if we could do
something behind the scenes,

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.100
but there's nothing we can use.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.140
What do we do?

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:43.530
At this rate, even if we can avoid their attacks with EW, if they catch us and dock, it's over.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.370
Then why don't we change our perspective a little?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.080
Junigh Coolph.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.920
Eldest son of Theodore Coolph,
Secretary of Interstellar Transportation.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.630
A spoiled rich kid who will someday be a politician.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.670
My uncle plans to marry me to Junigh,

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.260
and expand the company that way.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:10.260
Certainly, ties to the Interstellar Transportation
Bureau would confer an advantage.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.020
And he wants to make Jenny a politician's wife,

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.430
to keep her from the business.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:18.100
By changing our perspective,

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.560
you mean to go after the fiancé's weakness.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:25.110
If nothing else, we can get the marriage canceled.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.990
If they cancel it,

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.660
that would weaken her uncle's position.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.410
I see.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:33.780
Well, it's indirect, but...

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.450
This is only my personal opinion,

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.710
but I just don't like the guy.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.960
Why is that?

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:41.580
Intuition.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.250
A woman's intuition.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.510
It's a political marriage, anyway.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.220
I wouldn't mind doing it as camouflage.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.180
Oh, really?

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.180
No... No, I actually do!

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.430
I'd imagine so.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:58.640
I met him once, at a party.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.020
There was indeed something off about him.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.480
Yeah, something off.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.070
I understand that he's a bit off.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.440
Wow, she gets it!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.320
But that isn't enough.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.350
It's not a weakness.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.160
What do we do?

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:17.620
Anyone of the elite class is likely to have weaknesses, for better or for worse.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.000
Keep searching, and you'll find something.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.460
Morals are not of particular concern here.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.800
Coming from you, that sounds strangely convincing...

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.300
Weaknesses, hmm...

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.300
Once in a while,

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.470
Junigh hosts clandestine parties on his large, private ship.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.560
That might lead to something.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:38.890
Okay!

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:41.480
I have nothing against your fiancé,

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.230
but let's see what we can dig up!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.450
Robert Dolittle's a nasty guy.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.580
Former Stellar Military.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.580
Friends in politics and finance.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.460
If they underestimate him because

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.540
he only heads a company fleet, they might regret it.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.170
Large donations to volunteer groups.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:07.880
But lots of accusations of bribery.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.340
Hugh and Dolittle Board Member Suspected of Bribery

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.510
A hypocrite.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.800
There we go... Hugh and Dolittle's accounting records.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:20.180
The first security layer took a while, but once inside, it's easy.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.180
Nice.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:21.640
So, here.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.150
There's no record attached to this money.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.480
This amount...

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.190
I bet there are all kinds of neat things to find here.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.900
Found this too.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:37.950
Would you look...

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:38.780
...at that.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.870
Huh? Interesting right?

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:45.460
Yeah, let's have Show report this to the captain.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.420
For the time being, we've dodged them all.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.060
They're still jamming our attacks.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.270
Continue EW, and prepare to dock.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.480
Don't let them escape.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.700
They're all heading toward us!

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:17.740
I'll call Marika and the others!

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.410
Everyone,

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:20.950
I'm back!

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:21.870
Marika!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.870
Set course for the Totemstet Galaxy.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:29.500
We're heading for Jenny's fiancé's ship, The Glorious Coolph!

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.710
Let's get outta here.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.420
Roger!

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.680
President.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.890
I'd like to try what we discussed.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:44.850
Already on it.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.440
The pirate ship lies directly in front of us.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.190
Target their engines.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:52.940
Keep them from escaping.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.190
Combat teams, get to the docking port.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:59.120
Powered suit teams are ready for close quarters combat.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.740
All ships, continue firing on the pirate ship.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.910
This ship will prepare to dock and engage.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:29.230
We will be approaching the pirate ship shortly.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.860
There are now three Bentenmarus!

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.150
They're splitting off!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:33.900
What do you mean?

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:34.570
Analyzing!

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:38.700
Bentenmaru alpha has changed course, and is heading for us!

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.140
All three Bentenmarus have vanished.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.430
They've escaped.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.310
A quick vertical turnaround...

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.850
Give chase. Do not let them get away.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:07.270
Yes, sir.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.060
Wow.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.270
Hey, how did you do that?

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.770
We cloned ourselves.

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:18.190
Just kidding.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.900
Remember when we ran into

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.030
that ghost ship during our practice cruise?

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:29.500
That gave me the idea to create copies of the Bentenmaru's mass profile.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.080
Then, I merely loaded them and dummy transponders

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.710
onto two decoy missiles...

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.300
I get it.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.760
You were also great, Yayoi and Ai.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.880
You looked the Jabberwocky right in the face.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.140
The reactor was stable,

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.680
so I was able to maintain high acceleration.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.930
Everything else was Ai's piloting.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:49.930
Not at all...

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.810
Yayoi, you're amazing!

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.900
I'm impressed by how much you can coax from that engine.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.150
You too, Ai.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.150
Your piloting was fantastic.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.570
Thank you.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.950
Okay, everyone...

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.660
Let's make a run to The Glorious Coolph.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.710
Roger!

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.330
Marika,

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.370
a message from Show at the insurance company.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:11.870
Picking it up.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.830
Hey, how's it going?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.210
Looks like they've been shooting lots of lasers at you.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.920
Got a plan?

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:23.130
We're about to board Junigh Coolph's ship.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.550
I see.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:26.890
Nice plan, but the uncle's the real target, right?

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:27.510
I have some great info on Robert Dolittle here.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:30.850
100 Secrets of Robert
I have some great info on Robert Dolittle here.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.190
Ah, this?

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.120
Hugh and Dolittle's accounting records.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:40.530
Their security is as shoddy as ever.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.900
But who gave you this?

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.700
You shouldn't ask questions like that.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.160
I'll leave it to your imagination.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.420
You're being spoiled, Captain.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:58.750
And there's more!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.550
One more useful piece of information.

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.970
We've completed docking with The Glorious Coolph.

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:12.870
Roger!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.230
President, how's the connection?

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.480
Looking good.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.230
Don't screw up.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:18.730
Right!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.940
I hope he agrees.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.700
This should be a valuable card.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.700
If nothing else, we should be able to force him to negotiate.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:30.870
Yeah.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.870
Lilly, keep the camera rolling.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:33.660
Aye aye, sir!

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.120
The famous ship captain high schooler,
Kato Marika infiltrates
a mysterious cruiser!!

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.740
This is real time...

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:39.670
A live broadcast.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.090
A high school girl is hijacking the airwaves?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:46.260
Marika?

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:54.600
That's the party room, right?

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.270
It's strangely quiet.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:57.480
Is this the right place?

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:58.980
We'll know when we get there!

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:00.940
The time has come.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:09.780
The time has come to destroy the system and rise up!

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:10.240
<b>79th Smash the System Conference
Revo-Lution Junigh and you!</b>

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:14.660
We will start a revolution, in the name of justice!
<b>79th Smash the System Conference
Revo-Lution Junigh and you!</b>

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:14.830
We will start a revolution, in the name of justice!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:24.340
To the revolution!

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:39.020
How the hell can you call yourselves revolutionaries,

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:44.610
when you're too stupid to notice the pirate ship knocking down your front door?

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:48.780
Everyone, line up in front of me!
Miss Chiaki's been under a lot of stress.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.910
Maybe it's because she wasn't a pirate last time.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.830
I wanted to do it too!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:01.250
<i>News Flash!!
Anti-government Guerillas
Successfully Captured!!</i>

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:03.590
N-N-No!

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.960
This is just a hobby!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.380
We don't care about revolutions and coup d'états!

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.800
So don't kill me!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:11.970
Shut up.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.560
Sketchy, yeah...

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.600
Hello!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.100
This is Jenny Dolittle!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:21.060
I was planning on meeting my fiancé before the wedding.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.860
And look what I found!

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:23.690
<i>Shock!!
The Guerilla Leader Is a
Famous Politician's Son?</i>

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.360
No! No, I'm not...

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.070
<i>Shock!!
The Guerilla Leader Is a
Famous Politician's Son?</i>

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.070
Daddy!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.780
Junigh Coolph

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:30.490
Daddy!

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.740
A politician's son saying, "To the revolution"...

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:36.700
That's a pretty big scandal.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.710
This has been Jenny Dolittle!

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.840
This game is over.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.560
It's no use resisting.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.310
Come with me.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:03.900
No.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:09.690
Making a fuss here won't affect
anything with Hugh and Dolittle.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.700
You pirates can keep running your little shows.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:23.080
Actually, this is part of our business too.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.670
We are escorting Jenny to Space University.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.550
Tricks won't change

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.260
the situation.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:48.270
This contains data on Hugh and Dolittle.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:51.530
According to this, a lot of money is circulating with no clear purpose.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.650
What of it?

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:57.160
I have no intention of discussing
our company's internal affairs.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.660
Silent Whisper.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:03.370
Shout Blue.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.580
Jormungand.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:05.620
Phaser Arrow.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:13.130
Those are the names of the military craft and weapons you've been sending to this brat's father, Theodore Coolph.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.420
Right, Uncle?

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:20.510
And you've also been supplying weapons and fighters
to other groups opposing the Stellar Military.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:26.810
Just like pirates require licenses, there are strict limits as to who can possess weaponry.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.110
Not that you don't know,

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:32.570
but it's strictly forbidden for an individual politician to possess such weaponry.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:37.280
But a company buying them to improve security

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:39.160
is a sufficient excuse.

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:45.870
You transferred the weapons to Theodore Coolph,
and were paid in cash, in return.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:49.750
That's a crime, Uncle.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.210
Childish fantasies.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.200
<i>The ship-to-ship missile Jormungand, yes.</i>

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.340
<i>That might be difficult.</i>

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:58.970
Call with Theodore Coolph

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.510
<i>You can put a hundred pistachios on the receipt.</i>

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.310
You never deleted

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.890
those call logs.

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:07.850
Secret conferences to discuss weapon transfers.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.020
Got them right here.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.110
Cheers!

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:18.820
This time, it was close!

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:21.330
Maybe we <i>are</i> cut out to be pirates!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:23.700
The ad-lib job went perfectly.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:24.120
Yeah.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.290
Jeez...

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.500
You guys always get so caught up in this.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.830
But you were the most amazing of all.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:31.250
That's not true.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.170
That's the Barbalusa's daughter for you!

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.130
Shut up!

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.340
Um,

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:40.510
what will you do now,  Miss Chiaki?

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:42.390
You'll stay at Hakuoh, right?

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.390
No, I'm going back home.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.680
My dad's starting to nag me about it.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:47.730
I see.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:48.810
That's a shame.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:51.810
I wanted you to teach me more about the ship.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:56.230
Then let's have a farewell party for Chiaki too!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.940
Yeah!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.540
Thanks for everything, Captain.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.250
Really!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.500
You should warn me about these things in advance.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.750
Now I can finally go to Space University.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:20.300
When I graduate, I'll probably have to fight my uncle again.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:26.060
He'll be arrested for corruption and weapon trafficking,
but he'll probably pull some strings and get himself out.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:27.020
Really...

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:29.100
We're a family company after all.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:32.100
So he'll keep his position, most likely.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.400
I see.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.060
However,

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:37.980
I've learned a lot from you, so I can fight him.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.280
Even on my own.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:41.700
It's okay.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.870
From now on, I'll be with you forever.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.950
I won't let you fight by yourself.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.000
Lynn...

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:49.960
Jenny!

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:53.250
Let's show 'em.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.210
I've seen enough...

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.800
Hey, there's another one.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:03.510
"A big success for the Bentenmaru crew.
Hugh and Dolittle suspected of corruption," it says.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.930
This was a big deal.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.890
I never expected her to use the stuff we gave her like that.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.310
Women who don't fear anything are scary.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.230
That's right.

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:13.190
Yup.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:16.150
You shouldn't get on a woman's bad side.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.900
A-A lot happened. So, u-uh, good job!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:25.820
The captain and the other girls made it to the Odette II as well.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.330
Everyone, I have our exam results.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:30.370
We're all negative.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.160
We'll be released next week.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:32.870
All right!

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.170
I've been feeling stiff.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:35.880
Let's do this!

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:44.090
So that fighter...

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.510
Silent what was it?

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.050
You got to take it.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:53.020
Yeah, they said there's nothing
wrong with pirates having a fighter.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:57.980
It's in my name, but I left it at the relay station, so the yacht club can use it.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:02.190
Mami...

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:03.530
Thanks.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.450
For what?

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.990
All those clothes.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:07.740
You gave them to Gruier, right?

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:09.370
Oh, that.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:13.080
I just wanted to help.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:13.870
Thanks.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:15.920
You're welcome.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.170
So you'll be out of the hospital next week.

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:22.800
Yeah.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.840
Sorry for the trouble.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.510
No problem.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:29.810
I got to relax, so it was fine.

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:31.100
I'm glad.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:33.520
Enjoy your high school life while it lasts.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:35.350
I know.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:39.230
Hey, Misa.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.610
What?

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:41.860
Thanks.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:46.660
Oh, did I do something you should thank me for?

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:48.870
I just wanted to say it.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:49.530
Bye.

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:50.490
Goodbye.

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:56.790
The pot-au-feu is done.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:57.580
Right!

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:00.380
It looks great!

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:03.460
I made your favorite, some chikuwa!

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:04.970
I love chikuwa!

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.300
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:11.430
We'll Have Juice at the After Party

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:12.510
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:18.020
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:21.020
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:24.400
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:27.490
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:30.530
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:39.460
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:44.340
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:48.170
How far?

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.840
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:54.470
Until the end.

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:55.810
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:59.140
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:07.990
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:11.740
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:13.160
What should we do?

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:16.330
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:20.620
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:26.670
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.930
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:39.730 --> 00:23:41.390
With a big job behind her,

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:43.150
Kato Marika takes a short break.

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:46.790
But the Bentenmaru's crew remains in the hospital.

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:49.650
What new danger will attack Marika,

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:53.410
during the maintenance and cleaning of
the Odette II and the Bentenmaru?

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:56.330
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:57.290
The bonds among the four.

00:23:57.860 --> 00:23:59.000
Look forward to it.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.000
The Bonds Among the Four

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.340
I love chikuwa!
